      {label:'Place a market order for all 500 shares, just get in fast',outcome:'Terrible idea for this stock. With a $0.40 spread and thin volume, your 500-share market order will eat through the ask side, potentially filling at $18.70, $18.90, even $19.10. You could lose $300+ to slippage instantly.',correct:false},
      {label:'Place a limit order at $18.55 for 500 shares, be patient',outcome:'Smart move. Your limit order sits on the bid side, offering a better price than other buyers. You might wait a few hours, but you control your price. Even if it only partially fills, you avoid all slippage.',correct:true},
      {label:'Place five separate market orders for 100 shares each',outcome:'Splitting the order reduces impact slightly, but each fill still suffers the wide spread. Five market orders at the ask of $18.70 still overpays by $0.20/share. A single limit order at $18.55 is far more efficient.',correct:false}
