        { term: 'Herd Mentality', definition: 'The tendency to follow the crowd in investment decisions rather than making independent analysis-based choices, leading to buying high during euphoria and selling low during panic.', example: 'In late 2021, retail investors poured billions into meme stocks and crypto at peak prices because "everyone was doing it." Most lost 60-90% within a year.' },
        { term: 'Anchoring Bias', definition: 'The tendency to fixate on a specific reference point (like your purchase price) when making decisions, even when that reference point is irrelevant to the investment\'s current value.', example: 'Refusing to sell a stock that dropped from $100 to $40 because you\'re "waiting to break even", even though the company\'s business has fundamentally deteriorated.' },
        { term: 'FOMO', definition: 'Fear Of Missing Out, the anxiety that others are profiting from an opportunity you\'re not participating in, driving impulsive investment decisions without proper analysis.', example: 'Buying Bitcoin at $60,000 because your coworker bragged about doubling his money, then watching it crash to $16,000, the textbook FOMO cycle.' }
